WEBVTT

NOTE Release

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.112
Meet titus-humanizer, a new editing skill
for Claude and ChatGPT,

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:07.000
now published on GitHub.

NOTE Rewrite

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.177
Give it a draft that sounds like AI,

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:15.195
and it marks each pattern that gives the
draft away. The stock opener. The em dash.

00:00:15.195 --> 00:00:18.823
The framing that says it isn't just one
thing, it's another.

00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:21.000
And the clause tacked on at the end.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Then it rewrites the sentence in plain
words, and keeps every fact.

NOTE Score

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Each rewrite comes with a score from zero
to one, before and after.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.167
This sample email from the test suite
drops from 0.80 to 0.01,

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.000
with no patterns left.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.000
The score counts writing patterns. It
isn't an AI detector.

NOTE How it works

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.205
Here's how it works.

00:00:45.205 --> 00:00:49.000
First, it removes hidden characters, such
as zero-width spaces.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.000
It applies seven hard rules.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
It fixes wording that's awkward, flowery,
vague, unnecessary or illogical.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.000
It cuts story-level patterns.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.000
And it scores the original and the
rewrite.

NOTE Stories

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.459
It handles fiction, too.

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:07.436
Using the StoryScope study of AI-written
stories,

00:01:07.436 --> 00:01:11.873
it cuts weather that mirrors the mood,
fear told through body sensations,

00:01:11.873 --> 00:01:14.000
and morals the narrator spells out.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The rewrite keeps her decision and names
the feeling plainly.

NOTE Formats

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.483
Use it on emails, reports, slide decks,
résumés, papers and more.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:28.000
Résumé date ranges and bullets come
through intact.

NOTE Easiest install

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.537
The simplest way to install is to copy
this repository's link into Claude,

00:01:34.537 --> 00:01:40.000
Claude Code, ChatGPT, or Codex, and ask it
to help you install the skill.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.273
It will handle the installation for you,

00:01:42.273 --> 00:01:45.000
or walk you through any step it can't do
itself.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
To install it yourself, follow the steps
that come next.

NOTE Install in the app

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.065
To install it in the Claude app,

00:01:52.065 --> 00:01:56.000
first download the zip file from the
Releases page on GitHub.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
In Settings, open Capabilities, and turn
on Create and edit files.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.092
Then open Customize, then Skills.

00:02:02.092 --> 00:02:06.718
Click plus, choose Create skill, then
Upload a skill, and select the zip.

00:02:06.718 --> 00:02:09.000
Turn the skill on, and you're ready.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.824
In ChatGPT, go to Skills, select Create,

00:02:11.824 --> 00:02:15.000
and upload the same zip without unzipping
it.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.856
If your plan doesn't support skills,

00:02:17.856 --> 00:02:21.000
you can build a Custom GPT from the
instructions in the repo.

NOTE Install from the command line

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:23.852
In Claude Code,

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:28.000
two commands add the repo as a plugin
marketplace and install the plugin.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.486
For Codex, clone the repo,

00:02:30.486 --> 00:02:35.000
and copy the skill folder into the agents
skills folder in your home directory.

NOTE Get it

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.683
titus-humanizer works in Claude, Claude
Code, ChatGPT and Codex.

00:02:41.683 --> 00:02:46.000
It's free under the MIT license, and the
link is on screen.
